# LeakSanitizer suppressions for known, deliberate leaks.
#
# Use with:
#   LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=tools/dev/lsan.supp make test
#
# Every entry needs a reason. Do not add entries to hide new leaks, fix them.

# Packfile.set_string_native deserializes a PackFile and must not destroy it,
# because the PMCs created from its segments (e.g. sub->seg) still point into
# it. See the "XXX memory leak" comment in src/pmc/packfile.pmc. Needs
# reference counting of PackFile segments to be fixed properly.
leak:Parrot_Packfile_set_string_native

# PackfileBytecodeSegment.get_pointer builds a fresh PackFile_ByteCode on each
# call. When reached through PackfileDirectory the PackFile owns and frees it,
# but the get_addr op on a bare PackfileBytecodeSegment has no way to free it.
leak:Parrot_PackfileBytecodeSegment_get_pointer
